# Intent: the standing offline look (owner, 2026-11-13), driven by the firmware's own link state. While Home is out of reach the normal face stays and reacts locally, in a muted palette named "offline" (grey-blue, eyes 5 px lower; reserved for the firmware: the host's palette tool cannot pick it and it is never saved), with a small strip in the top-left corner (the slash glyph and "Offline") instead of a speech bubble the mint skin does not have. After 3 s down a connecting strip shows (the bars cycling, no words); after 10 s the offline look and the existing dim amber ring; when the session opens the saved palette, the glyph and the words are removed. "Can't reach Home" on a tap while offline now rides on the strip for 3 s. hal_bridge gets hub_link_set(connecting, offline, refused) and link_note(text); offline_indicator and offline_indicator_refresh (patch 075's bubble writes) are removed.
# Upstream: m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/stackchan/avatar/skins/mint/mint.cpp, hal/board/ (stackchan_display, hal_bridge, stackchan.cc) and 78/xiaozhi-esp32 main/application.cc, main/protocols/websocket_protocol.cc (MIT). Applies after 111.
# Check after a flash: stop Home: after about 3 s a Wi-Fi glyph cycles in the corner, after 10 s the face goes grey-blue with the slash glyph and "Offline" and the ring shows dim amber; tap the face: the doubt face and "Can't reach Home" for 3 s, then back to "Offline"; start Home: the colours, the strip and the amber ring clear and the host's palette (or night) is back.
